  "known_local_policies": [
    "Each Gambit stage requires three distinct original Fire/Frost/Arcane CAST schools after that stage activates. Existing normal/countered hand cast-attempt policy is reused; failed automatic attempts and other actors do not count.",
    "Quest rewards use one original physical Spell draw, ordinary current-class discovery from the full union of those three schools, and the original fixed 5-mana 7/7 Arcanist reward. No unsupported per-school menu quota is inferred from card text.",
    "Stage display faces retain full original records but are choice-only, cost-hidden, not hand playable, and have no pool metadata or generated membership.",
    "Dawngrasp uses the existing independent persistent player Spell Damage +3 program; independent successful battlecries stack and survive minion departure and hero changes.",
    "Wildfire uses the already implemented two ordinary named phases and a permanent friendly HERO_POWER HealthRule on the current hero, preserving source identity and original replacement/attachment lifecycle.",
    "Quest phase, countered cast, discovery class and hand-capacity reward windows remain explicit local policies pending CN calibration. Version/hotfix alignment and edge-rule testing are deferred."
